# Native plugin binaries. *.dll was already tracked; the macOS and Linux
# equivalents were not. Adding a pattern only affects files written from now
# on, so blobs already in history stay plain until they are rewritten.
#
# Only the two unambiguous native shared-object extensions are listed. *.lib is
# deliberately excluded: Explorer/Assets/Scenes/TestJsScenes/sdk6-basic-scene/
# bin/game.js.lib is JavaScript, and an LFS rule would rewrite it as a pointer.
*.dylib filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.so filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# The out-of-process decode child, shipped beside the client library. It is the
# one native binary that no extension rule catches: on macOS it has none at all,
# and *.exe is unmatched. uuav-verify.yml's LFS enforcement only diffs
# *.dll|*.dylib|*.so, so without these two lines the first committed adapter
# would land as a plain ~1 MB blob and grow the pack on every rebuild. Landed
# before any binary does, because an attribute added afterwards does not
# retroactively convert.
uuav-adapter filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
uuav-adapter.exe filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text


